  urldate = {2024-02-06},
  abstract = {Kurdish has pre-, circum- and, in some dialects, postpositions. Common traits and variation of adpositions in Kurdish are discussed using MDKD material. The inventory of adpositions in Kurdish is composed of a relatively small set of core and other adpositions, including several types of compound adpositions. There is considerable variation, with parts of the south (mostly prepositions) and the north (more postpositions) as extreme ends. Shared combinations of prepositions and a pronominal element are preserved or, in some dialects, reanalysed as forms used with clitic pronouns. Variation is also found in meaning, and items may overlap with other adpositions and means of expressing semantic functions. Area-particular features are found across neighbouring varieties in both Northern and Central Kurdish.},
